phase P4
title Core
description
    **Class:** verifiable.

    **Kind:** feature.

    **Goal:** the production runtime for what the prototypes proved, in
    `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`, built from the core Specs with the prototype open beside it, one
    module at a time: Compiled and the compiler; lane, step and turn; the persistence edge,
    write-ahead and the driver; restore and key versions; fragments; operations; the CLI's `check`,
    `explain` and `graph`.

    **Starts when:** interleaved with P3 by area (the Epic's instructions): each module starts once
    its area's suite is proven and audited; T15's cross-area audit gates T23.

    **Verified by:**

    - P3's suite through a production adapter (coverage record in @plan.Runtime);
    - skill:check-task per Task;
    - `nub run check` at zero;
    - `nub run verify`.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task: build it against its Spec, check it independently,
    repair. The Pay path first, end to end, as the walking skeleton.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - the suite passes on the production runtime alone, the prototype adapter retired;
    - every gate fails on its broken runtime;
    - `nub run verify` passes;
    - the completion audit passes.

    **False pass:** the production adapter doing work the runtime should.

    **Caught by:** mutants run against the production adapter, and a review section on the adapter's
    role.

    **Gates:**

    - falsify on the production adapter;
    - one probe file per lint rule that `nub run check` must reject (`tools/lint-bomb/`).

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - public entry-point names;
    - a large public API change;
    - a guarantee that can't be met;
    - a guarantee change.

    **User's read:** the internal module layout; small public API calls.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-testing: test first, module integration tests through the public interface (no
      unit tests of internals), and the scenarios that enforce each Invariant written before the code;
    - skill:playbook-build (long runs);
    - skill:execute-task;
    - skill:check-task;
    - skill:to-design per module;
    - skill:review;
    - skill:diagnose when a case fails unexplained.
tasks
    T16
        title       The Pay path end to end on production
        status      in_progress
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T6, @task.V3.T7, @task.V3.T8, @task.V3.T13]
        description
            Build the thinnest production runtime that runs checkout's Pay machine through the public API and the
            production adapter: the walking skeleton.

            **Why now:** P4 has no production code yet, and every later module needs one path that runs end to
            end to build on.

            **Read first:** @spec.Compile, @spec.Turn, @spec.WriteLanes,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/port.ts#Port,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/fixtures/pay.ts#Pay. Blocked by the suite areas the Pay
            path uses (@task.V3.T6, @task.V3.T7, @task.V3.T8, @task.V3.T13), not by T15; if T15's audit
            weakens a Pay oracle, T16 is repaired against it.

            - **May change:** `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`, the production adapter.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** the adapter doing runtime work → caught by mutants on the adapter.
            - **Gates:** P3's suite, Pay cases; `nub run check`.
            - **Stops:** public entry-point names.
            - **User's read:** module layout.
        acceptance
            The Pay cases pass on production through the Port; their mutants are killed.
